# Line endings are provenance here, not style.
#
# `manifest.json` records a SHA-256 of the gold CSV it was run against, and the
# report is meant to be reproducible from that hash. When a file is written with
# CRLF and git normalises it to LF on commit, the committed manifest and the
# committed dataset no longer agree -- silently, and in a way that makes a
# correct provenance check look like tampering. It happened once already.
#
# So the bytes on disk are the bytes in the object database.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.xlsx binary
